    "fullText": "The Puranas\r\n    \r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4e3b2;\r\n            color: #4b2a2a;\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 0;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        header {\r\n            background-color: #a85a32;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        h1, h2 {\r\n            color: #a85a32;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .content {\r\n            max-width: 800px;\r\n            margin: 20px auto;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            background-color: #fff8e7;\r\n            box-shadow: 0px 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .section {\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        footer {\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            background-color: #a85a32;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n        }\r\n    \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    The Puranas\r\n    Ancient Texts of Hindu Cosmology, Mythology, and Philosophy\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n        Introduction to the Puranas\r\n        The Puranas are a genre of ancient Hindu texts that encompass a wide array of topics, including cosmology, mythology, genealogies, history, and spiritual teachings. Composed in Sanskrit, the Puranas serve as a guide to Hindu philosophy and culture, preserving the essence of dharma, rituals, and legends of gods, sages, and heroes. The Puranas are often classified into 18 Mahapuranas (Major Puranas) and 18 Upapuranas (Minor Puranas).\r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n        The 18 Mahapuranas\r\n        The 18 Mahapuranas, regarded as the core Puranic texts, are traditionally divided into three groups of six, each focused on one of the Trimurti: Brahma, Vishnu, and Shiva.\r\n        \r\n            Brahma Puranas\r\n                \r\n                    Brahma Purana\r\n                    Brahmanda Purana\r\n                    Brahmavaivarta Purana\r\n                    Markandeya Purana\r\n                    Bhavishya Purana\r\n                    Vamana Purana\r\n                \r\n            \r\n            Vishnu Puranas\r\n                \r\n                    Vishnu Purana\r\n                    Bhagavata Purana\r\n                    Narada Purana\r\n                    Garuda Purana\r\n                    Padma Purana\r\n                    Varaha Purana\r\n                \r\n            \r\n            Shiva Puranas\r\n                \r\n                    Shiva Purana\r\n                    Linga Purana\r\n                    Skanda Purana\r\n                    Agni Purana\r\n                    Matsya Purana\r\n                    Kurma Purana\r\n                \r\n            \r\n        \r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n        Major Themes in the Puranas\r\n        \r\n            Cosmology: Puranas provide detailed descriptions of the universe’s creation, structure, and cycles of cosmic time, often portraying the universe as evolving through various cycles of creation and destruction.\r\n            History: The Puranas narrate stories of gods, goddesses, sages, and demons, weaving moral and philosophical lessons through rich and symbolic narratives.\r\n            Genealogy: They include genealogies of gods, royal dynasties, sages, and mythological figures, connecting different eras and forming a comprehensive mytho-historical framework.\r\n            Rituals and Pilgrimage: The Puranas outline rituals, festivals, and the significance of sacred places, guiding devotees in their spiritual practices.\r\n        \r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n        The 18 Upapuranas\r\n        The Upapuranas are considered secondary Puranic texts. While not as widely known as the Mahapuranas, they cover similar themes and provide additional narratives and instructions on spirituality, dharma, and culture. Some of the notable Upapuranas include:\r\n        \r\n            Sanatkumara Purana\r\n            Durvasa Purana\r\n            Narasimha Purana\r\n            Shiva Rahasya Purana\r\n            Kalika Purana\r\n            Bhargava Purana\r\n        \r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n        The Role of the Puranas in Hindu Culture\r\n        The Puranas have shaped Hindu culture, providing narratives that simplify complex Vedic teachings and making them accessible to all. They emphasize dharma (righteous living) and explore themes of devotion (*bhakti*), karma, and cosmology, enabling spiritual and moral growth. The stories and teachings found in the Puranas continue to inspire art, literature, and social values in Hindu society.\r\n    \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    &copy; 2023 - Understanding the Puranas and Their Significance"
